Z||000000||The Aura||11-21-2001||03:40 PM||||Is it true that the Chevy Citation Front struts lower the back of the fiero when used on the rear? Has anyone out there done this... were you pleased w/ the results?<BR><P>------------------<BR>1986 GT 4spd&gt; Suspension Techniques Springs, Poly Bushings, Bosal Brospeed 4.5" Exhaust Tips||||reg||3
Z||000001||Mr.Frosty||11-21-2001||03:50 PM||||I did it just recently.I'm happy with the results.I changed them out at the same time I did my lowering springs,so I'm not sure how much it lowered it,but the back end dropped 2 inches,and the springs were only supposed to drop it 1.5" inches.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT Turbo intercooled||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mr.Frosty||11-21-2001||03:51 PM||||I'll take some pics as soon as I get the new end link rod from the dealer.It's up on one jack stand right now.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT Turbo intercooled||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mark||11-21-2001||07:04 PM||||I once compared the citation and fiero struts side-by-side and yes, the spring perch on the citction struts are about 1/2 inch or so lower on the barrel of the strut.  I was leary about buying citation struts however, since I have only about 1/2 inch clearance between the inner edge of my rear tires (stock '86 GT, 215/60-15) and the spring perch on the OEM fiero struts.  I'm thinking the 14" wheels may offer more clearance here.  Anyone else have clearance info for this mod?  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||lowCG||11-23-2001||12:54 PM||||I first did this to try and use a replaceable strut cartridge/insert,with the 14" rims a few years back.<BR>Now,with 16" rims,I just welded the tops of some threaded struts to the top of my Fiero ones and used some bilsteins from a VW.<BR>Don't know for sure if they'll interfere with non-stock wheels.||||reg||1
